        title: "Infectious Disease Coding",
        content: `**ICD-10-CM Chapter 1 (A00-B99)** covers **infectious and parasitic diseases** — the highest-stakes chapter on the CCA. Sequencing errors here trigger denials, audits, and inaccurate severity-of-illness reporting.

This lesson drills the four scenarios that dominate CCA test items: **sepsis** (always two codes — the underlying infection PLUS R65.21 when septic shock is present), **HIV/AIDS** (B20 takes principal status whenever the admission is HIV-related; Z21 is reserved for **asymptomatic** carriers), **MRSA** (Z16.11 reports antibiotic resistance and drives contact precautions), and **COVID-19** (U07.1 for confirmed cases, Z20.822 for contact or suspected exposure that turns out negative).

Master the sequencing logic, and you will defend every audit with confidence.`,
