      {
        type: "application",
        title: "Putting CPT to Work as a CCA",
        content: `As a **CCA-credentialed outpatient coder**, you will read provider documentation and select the **single CPT** that best describes each billable service. Your daily workflow:

1. **Open the encounter** in the EHR / abstraction queue.
2. **Identify each billable service** — E/M visit, procedure, lab, imaging.
3. **Look up the CPT** in the appropriate section (use the **Index**, then verify in the **Tabular**).
4. **Check Category I first**; only fall back to **Category III** if no Category I exists for an emerging technology.
5. **Apply modifiers** — start with **-25/-59** decisions, then sequence anatomic modifiers (**-LT, -RT, -50**).
6. **Run NCCI edits** before claim submission.

**CCA exam tip:** Memorize the **6 section ranges** cold. Questions often start with *"In which CPT section would you find code 71046?"* — that's a chest X-ray, in **Radiology (70010–79999)**. Recognizing the range tells you the section without needing the codebook.`,
        visual: {
          type: "diagram",
          svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="70" font-family="Arial" font-size="40" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Coder Daily Workflow</text><rect x="100" y="120" width="900" height="120" fill="#6366f1" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="165" font-family="Arial" font-size="22" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">1. Open encounter</text><text x="550" y="200" font-family="Arial" font-size="17" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle">Review provider note + orders</text><text x="550" y="225" font-family="Arial" font-size="22" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle">↓</text><rect x="100" y="260" width="900" height="120" fill="#10b981" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="305" font-family="Arial" font-size="22" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">2. Identify billable services</text><text x="550" y="340" font-family="Arial" font-size="17" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle">E/M? Procedure? Lab? Imaging?</text><text x="550" y="365" font-family="Arial" font-size="22" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle">↓</text><rect x="100" y="400" width="900" height="120" fill="#0ea5e9" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="445" font-family="Arial" font-size="22" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">3. Index → Tabular lookup</text><text x="550" y="480" font-family="Arial" font-size="17" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle">Never code from the Index alone</text><text x="550" y="505" font-family="Arial" font-size="22" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle">↓</text><rect x="100" y="540" width="900" height="120" fill="#8b5cf6" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="585" font-family="Arial" font-size="22" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">4. Category I first, III if none</text><text x="550" y="620" font-family="Arial" font-size="17" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle">Cat II = quality data (optional)</text><text x="550" y="645" font-family="Arial" font-size="22" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle">↓</text><rect x="100" y="680" width="900" height="120" fill="#ec4899" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="725" font-family="Arial" font-size="22" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">5. Apply modifiers</text><text x="550" y="760" font-family="Arial" font-size="17" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle">-25/-59 first, then -LT/-RT/-50</text><text x="550" y="785" font-family="Arial" font-size="22" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle">↓</text><rect x="100" y="820" width="900" height="180" fill="#f59e0b" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="870" font-family="Arial" font-size="22" fill="#1a1a2e" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">6. NCCI scrub → clean claim</text><text x="550" y="910" font-family="Arial" font-size="17" fill="#1a1a2e" text-anchor="middle">Catch bundling BEFORE the payer does</text><text x="550" y="950" font-family="Arial" font-size="17" fill="#1a1a2e" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Clean claim target ≥ 95%</text><text x="550" y="985" font-family="Arial" font-size="15" fill="#1a1a2e" text-anchor="middle">Memorize the 6 section ranges cold</text></svg>`,
          caption: "Six-step workflow every CCA-credentialed outpatient coder follows."
        }
      }
