        content: `The **Pathology and Laboratory section** of CPT covers every blood draw analysis, urine test, biopsy interpretation, and microbiology culture. The section spans **80047-89398** and is organized into clinically useful subsections that every HIM coder must recognize:

- **Organ/Disease-Oriented Panels** (80047-80081) — bundled groups
- **Drug Assay** (80305-80377) — qualitative and quantitative drug screens
- **Therapeutic Drug Assays** (80143-80299) — drug level monitoring
- **Chemistry** (82000-84999) — single chemistry tests
- **Hematology and Coagulation** (85002-85999) — blood cell and clotting tests
- **Microbiology** (87001-87999) — cultures, sensitivities, viral testing
- **Anatomic Pathology** (88000-88099) — postmortem
- **Cytopathology and Surgical Pathology** (88104-88399)

Key rule: **panel codes** bundle specific listed components — and the **all-or-nothing rule** governs whether you can use them.`,
